From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rajaryan1492007 <rajaryan1492007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:34:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] spirv: Don't implicitly set ACCESS_NON_WRITEABLE for input
 attachments

Khronos recently clarified that input attachments should be treated as
READ_WRITE_IMAGE_BIT in descriptor heaps, because current shader compilers
do not emit the NonWritable decoration for them.

VTN selects the resource type (read-only vs read-write) based on
ACCESS_NON_WRITEABLE when determining var->var->data.resource_type.
Implicitly forcing ACCESS_NON_WRITEABLE caused input attachments to be
marked read-only, which broke descriptor heap lowering (e.g. in RADV)
where the lowering expects matching read-write mappings.

Removing this implicit flag ensures VTN sets var->var->data.resource_type
correctly unless explicitly decorated with NonWritable by the application.

Ref: Khronos issue #4948, VVL PR #12976
Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/15987
Cc: mesa-stable
(cherry picked from commit 46744ba2134b19e766c4ddb9a82ac34980400903)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44489>
(cherry picked from commit 076b75387dd19a49b1037ab648ce9c1bb6e422a6)
---
 src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c b/src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c
index e9607d0caaf..399a6e35aac 100644
--- a/src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c
+++ b/src/compiler/spirv/vtn_variables.c
@@ -1637,7 +1637,6 @@ var_decoration_cb(struct vtn_builder *b, struct vtn_value *val, int member,
       return;
    case SpvDecorationInputAttachmentIndex:
       vtn_var->input_attachment_index = dec->operands[0];
-      vtn_var->access |= ACCESS_NON_WRITEABLE;
       return;
    case SpvDecorationAlignment:
       var_set_alignment(b, vtn_var, dec->operands[0]);
